  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "At the start of the first year, Sam has $\\$10$ in a bank account. At the end of every year, the bank pays 10% interest, and then Sam deposits another $\\$10$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p29-q-continuation-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Let $a_n$ be Sam’s balance, in dollars, at the start of the $n$th year. Find a recursive equation for $a_{n+1}$ in terms of $a_n$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a_{n+1}=1.1a_n+10$",
          "worked": "Interest is added before the deposit.\n$$\\begin{align*}a_{n+1}&=a_n+0.1a_n+10\\\\a_{n+1}&=1.1a_n+10.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q-continuation-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find a general formula for $a_n$ in terms of $n$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a_n=100(1.1)^n-100$ dollars.\n\nUse $a_n=p(1.1)^{n-1}+q$ and the first two balances to determine $p$ and $q$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a_1&=10\\\\a_2&=1.1(10)+10\\\\a_2&=21.\\end{align*}$$\nWrite $a_n=p(1.1)^{n-1}+q$. The first two terms give\n$$\\begin{align*}10&=p+q\\\\21&=1.1p+q.\\end{align*}$$\nSubtracting gives $11=0.1p$, so $p=110$ and $q=-100$. Hence\n$$\\begin{align*}a_n&=110(1.1)^{n-1}-100\\\\a_n&=100(1.1)^n-100.\\end{align*}$$\nThe balance is in dollars.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
  },
